This product statically links third-party software whose licenses require
attribution and, in the case of LGPL-2.1 components, the ability for the
end user to relink against a modified version of the library. Source for
those components is pinned in this repository's build system; the
`zig build` recipe rebuilds the binary from source. See
THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md for the full list, pinned versions, license texts,
and links to upstream source.

Statically-linked third-party components:

  - libcrun 1.23 (https://github.com/containers/crun, files under
    `src/libcrun/` and `libocispec/`; vendored under `vendor/crun-1.23/`)
    LGPL-2.1-or-later

  - libseccomp 2.5.6 (https://github.com/seccomp/libseccomp)
    LGPL-2.1-only

  - libcap 2.76 (https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/libs/libcap/libcap.git)
    BSD-3-Clause (selected from the BSD/GPL-2.0 dual-license offer)

  - yajl (https://github.com/lloyd/yajl), embedded in libcrun under
    `libocispec/yajl/` and built via the `--enable-embedded-yajl` knob
    ISC

  - argp-standalone 1.5.0 (https://github.com/argp-standalone/argp-standalone)
    LGPL-2.1-or-later

  - BLAKE3 (embedded in libcrun under `src/blake3/`)
    CC0-1.0 OR Apache-2.0

  - musl libc (Zig-bundled) (https://musl.libc.org/)
    MIT

`libsystemd` and `libcriu` are explicitly disabled at libcrun build
time (HAVE_SYSTEMD=0, HAVE_CRIU=0 in `build/cdeps/crun/config.h`). The
released rind binary contains no GPL-only components — see the per-file
LGPL audit table in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md.

The CLI half of `containers/crun` (its `src/{crun,run,create,start,…}.c`
top-level entry points, GPL-licensed upstream) is **not** vendored or
linked. Only the `src/libcrun/` library half — the half we statically
link — lives under `vendor/crun-1.23/`.
